{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>White cotton.</b> This verse is connected to what is above, in showing it, and the verse \"when it was full\" entered between them, like \"say to the boy\" and \"let him pass before us.\"" "<b>White.</b> It is a color, and it is white, from the root of \"the Horites,\" and so too in Aramaic." "<b>Cotton.</b> It is like its counterpart in Kedarite language. Also tekhelet is known, and these are colors in silk, and the proof is אחוז." "<b>By cords.</b> The ḥet has a pataḥ gadol. It is not like חֲבָלֵי יוֹלֵדָה." "<b>Buẓ.</b> It is linen. The Fatimites [grow] flax in Egypt; also purple, in wool." "<b>Rings.</b> Like גַּלְגַּלֵּי, as I will explain in the Mishkan of Solomon [Song of Songs 3:9–10]." "<b>Pillars of shesh.</b> Like marble [שֵׁשׁ]. And so עָשׂ and עִישׁ. Now the rings were between pillar and pillar, and some of them were covered by the aforementioned [materials]." "<b>Pavement.</b> Like \"stone pavement\" [מַרְצֵפַת אֲבָנִים], and they are the lower floor below." "<b>Bahat.</b> Also dar and soḥaret are precious stones."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra likens the syntactic interruption to 1 Samuel 9:27, where a narrative break occurs between two connected elements.", 3 "Ibn Ezra distinguishes the vocalization of חבלי here from the construct form with hatef-pataḥ found in Isaiah 37:3."}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:44.402563467Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}